        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sir John Wedderburn, 5th Baronet of Blackness; Charles Edward Stuart\n- Events: Jacobite uprising of 1745; Battle of Culloden\n- Places: Perthshire; Great Britain\n- Concepts: treason; restoration of the Stuart family to the throne\n\nFacts:\n- In 1745, Charles Edward Stuart instigated the unsuccessful Jacobite uprising and led an insurrection to restore his family to the throne of Great Britain.\n- Sir John Wedderburn, 5th Baronet of Blackness, was a Perthshire gentleman who joined Charles Edward Stuart's 1745 rebellion.\n- Sir John Wedderburn, 5th Baronet of Blackness, was captured at the Battle of Culloden.\n- After the Battle of Culloden, Sir John Wedderburn, 5th Baronet of Blackness, was convicted of treason.",
